{"type": "say", "text": "Hi everyone. Since the recommendation API is launching tomorrow morning, I'd like to get the caching and failover policy finalized and signed off today. The current draft uses the platform's default unscoped project-key cache policy and fails closed during an origin outage. Before I make any changes or sign off, I want to make sure we've got application and reliability perspectives weighed in. Does anyone have concerns with the current draft, or are we comfortable proceeding with sign-off?"}
